      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T12:05:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So then this patch does force DoH, and thus it\u0027s not \"Allow all DoH providers\", and more \"Force DoH if available for provider\".\n\nThat\u0027s not good. But then again, we shouldn\u0027t change the basic Android UI, so that doesn\u0027t leave many good options here.",
      "parentUuid": "b2455871_6df1f862",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d59daa8_32a55f85",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000062
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-30T14:33:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The URL we are generating in this patch isn\u0027t part of [RFC 8484](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8484) - `/dns-query` is commonly used, but not guaranteed. Today, browsers that allow you to configure DoH require you to give them a full URL. See Mullvad\u0027s guide as an example: https://mullvad.net/en/help/dns-over-https-and-dns-over-tls#browsers\n\nSo, rather than guessing at the URL, couldn\u0027t we just accept a full URL, and then if the user-provided string starts with https://, use DoH with what they gave us?",
      "parentUuid": "486b2183_ad0fa5ff",
      "revId": "528d633d21988272c64b1e094d075b1ab5d2fc1b",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
